  "note": "The feet-up table row (table_row_feet_up) on gym rings: ring_row's straps from the ceiling, hung low, the rings 75 cm up so the back just clears the floor at straight arms, the heels on the edge of a 46-cm bed in line with them, the ankles 130 cm from the rings; the hands hold the rings' bottoms, the fingers toward the head and clear of the straps. At the bottom the arms hang straight under the rings and the chin is tucked a little so the helm clears the floor; at the top the body is flat from the heels, the chest at the hands and the elbows past the ribs, the shoulder blades squeezed. About 73 % of the body on the hands at the bottom and 75 % at the top, from the vertical forces at the hands and the heels (Vural 2023 measured 73-76 % for a strap row with the feet up). The fault drops the hips (hips_sag), its stop line's break."
